  "Question": "Calculate: \\(20 \\div 0.4 = ?\\) (Give your answer as a decimal.)",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "50",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(40\\%\\) of a number is 20. Multiply both the dividend and divisor by 10 to make the divisor an integer without changing the quotient:\n\\[\n20 \\div 0.4 = 200 \\div 4 = 50.\n\\]\nThe number is 50. Written as a decimal, the answer is \\(50.0\\).",
